Step 12: Understanding Autoscale

The module introduced Autoscale.

Autoscale automatically adjusts the number of running VMs based on demand.

Example:

Low traffic:

2 Virtual Machines

High traffic:

10 Virtual Machines
Benefits:
Improved performance
Cost optimization
Automatic workload management

Autoscale is one of the most important cloud-native capabilities in Azure.

Step 13: Configuring Autoscale

The training demonstrated Autoscale configuration.

Common metrics:
Metric	Example Trigger
CPU Usage	Above 70%
Memory Usage	High utilization
Network Traffic	Increased demand
Queue Length	Growing workload
Example Rule:
If CPU > 70%

Add 2 VMs
Scale-In Example:
If CPU < 30%

Remove 1 VM
Benefits:
Dynamic scaling
Reduced operational effort
Better cost control

The module emphasized creating balanced scaling policies.

